{
 "0001": {
  "title": "",
  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_01\" id=\"tag_17_710_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "socket — create an endpoint for communication",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_02\" id=\"tag_17_710_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     19,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">sys/socket.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint socket(int</tt> <i>domain</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>type</i><tt>, int</tt> <i>protocol</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_03\" id=\"tag_17_710_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]socket[/I5]() function shall create an unbound socket in a communications domain, and return a file descriptor that can be\nused in later function calls that operate on sockets. The file descriptor shall be allocated as described in [A6][I7]2.6 File Descriptor Allocation[/I7][/A6].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A6": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/V2_chap02.html#tag_16_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I8]socket[/I8]() function takes the following arguments:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00008",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[I9]domain[/I9]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00009",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the communications domain in which a socket is to be created.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00010",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[I10]type[/I10]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00011",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the type of socket to be created.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00012",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[I11]protocol[/I11]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00013",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     5,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Specifies a particular protocol to be used with the socket. Specifying a [I12]protocol[/I12] of 0 causes [I13]socket[/I13]() to use an\nunspecified default protocol appropriate for the requested socket type.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The [I14]domain[/I14] argument specifies the address family used in the communications domain. The address families supported by the\nsystem are implementation-defined.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00015",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Symbolic constants that can be used for the domain argument are defined in the [A15][I16]&lt;sys/socket.h&gt;[/I16][/A15] header.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A15": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The [I17]type[/I17] argument specifies the socket type, which determines the semantics of communication over the socket. The\nfollowing socket types are defined; implementations may specify additional socket types:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00017",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     3
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_STREAM",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00018",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Provides sequenced, reliable, bidirectional, connection-mode byte streams, and may provide a transmission mechanism for\nout-of-band data.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00019",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     7
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_DGRAM",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00020",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Provides datagrams, which are connectionless-mode, unreliable messages of fixed maximum length.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00021",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     11
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_SEQPACKET",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00022",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     13,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Provides sequenced, reliable, bidirectional, connection-mode transmission paths for records. A record can be sent using one or more\noutput operations and received using one or more input operations, but a single operation never transfers part of more than one\nrecord. Record boundaries are visible to the receiver via the MSG_EOR flag.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00023",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     15
    ],
    "text": "Additionally, the [I18]type[/I18] argument can contain the bitwise-inclusive OR of flags from the following list:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00024",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     3
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_CLOEXEC",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00025",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Atomically set the FD_CLOEXEC flag on the new file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00026",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     7
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_CLOFORK",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00027",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Atomically set the FD_CLOFORK flag on the new file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00028",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     11
    ],
    "text": "SOCK_NONBLOCK",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00029",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     17,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Set the O_NONBLOCK file status flag on the new file description.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00030",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     19
    ],
    "text": "Implementations may define additional flags.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00031",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     21
    ],
    "text": "If the [I19]protocol[/I19] argument is non-zero, it shall specify a protocol that is supported by the address family. If the\n[I20]protocol[/I20] argument is zero, the default protocol for this address family and type shall be used. The protocols supported by\nthe system are implementation-defined.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00032",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23,
     23
    ],
    "text": "The process may need to have appropriate privileges to use the [I21]socket[/I21]() function or to create some sockets.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I21": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00033",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     25
    ],
    "text": "[A22][/A22]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A22": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_04\" id=\"tag_17_710_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00034",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     27,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I23]socket[/I23]() shall return a non-negative integer, the socket file descriptor. Otherwise, a value\nof -1 shall be returned and [I24]errno[/I24] set to indicate the error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00035",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29
    ],
    "text": "[A25][/A25]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A25": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_05\" id=\"tag_17_710_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00036",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I26]socket[/I26]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00037",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EAFNOSUPPORT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00038",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The implementation does not support the specified address family.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00039",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EMFILE]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00040",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "All file descriptors available to the process are currently open.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00041",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[ENFILE]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00042",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "No more file descriptors are available for the system.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00043",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EPROTONOSUPPORT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00044",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The value of [I27]protocol[/I27] is non-zero and either the protocol is not supported by the address family or the protocol is not\nsupported by the implementation.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00045",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[EPROTOTYPE]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00046",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The value of [I28]protocol[/I28] is non-zero and the socket type is not supported by the protocol.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00047",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[ESOCKTNOSUPPORT] \n[S29][[A30]OB[/A30]][/S29]\n[IMG31]\nor [EPROTONOSUPPORT] or [EPROTOTYPE]\n[IMG32]\n\n\n\nThe socket type is not supported by the address family, or the socket type is not supported by the implementation.",
    "placeholders": {
     "S29": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;OB&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG31": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG32": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00048",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I33]socket[/I33]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00049",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EACCES]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00050",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The process does not have appropriate privileges.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00051",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[ENOBUFS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00052",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Insufficient resources were available in the system to perform the operation.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00053",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[ENOMEM]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00054",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     31,
     7,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Insufficient memory was available to fulfill the request.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00055",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     37
    ],
    "text": "[A34][/A34]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_06\" id=\"tag_17_710_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00056",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     39,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00057",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41
    ],
    "text": "[A35][/A35]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A35": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_07\" id=\"tag_17_710_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00058",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The documentation for specific address families specifies which protocols each address family supports. The documentation for\nspecific protocols specifies which socket types each protocol supports.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00059",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The application can determine whether an address family is supported by trying to create a socket with [I36]domain[/I36] set to the\nprotocol in question.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00060",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45
    ],
    "text": "[A37][/A37]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A37": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_08\" id=\"tag_17_710_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00061",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     47,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The use of the SOCK_CLOEXEC and SOCK_CLOFORK flags in the [I38]type[/I38] argument of [I39]socket[/I39]() is necessary to avoid a data\nrace in multi-threaded applications. Without SOCK_CLOFORK, a file descriptor is leaked into a child process created by one thread\nin the window between another thread calling [I40]socket[/I40]() and using [A41][I42]fcntl[/I42]()[/A41] to set\nthe FD_CLOFORK flag. Without SOCK_CLOEXEC, a file descriptor intentionally inherited by child processes is similarly leaked into an\nexecuted program if FD_CLOEXEC is not set atomically. The SOCK_NONBLOCK flag is for convenience in avoiding additional [A43][I44]fcntl[/I44]()[/A43] calls.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I39": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A41": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I42": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A43": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00062",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     47,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Historically the standard did not specify the [I45]errno[/I45] value to be used when the socket type is not supported, and there\nwere differences between implementations. Some reused the existing standard [EPROTONOSUPPORT] or [EPROTOTYPE] values while others\nset [I46]errno[/I46] to a (then) non-standard value of [ESOCKTNOSUPPORT]. All three values are permitted in this version of the\nstandard, but the use of [EPROTONOSUPPORT] or [EPROTOTYPE] is considered to be misleading when no protocol is specified (that is,\nthe value of [I47]protocol[/I47] is zero) and consequently those alternatives have been marked obsolescent. If [I48]protocol[/I48] is\nnon-zero, since there is no precedence between error conditions, all three values will still be permitted even after the\nobsolescent alternatives for the [ESOCKTNOSUPPORT] condition have been removed.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I45": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I48": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00063",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     49
    ],
    "text": "[A49][/A49]FUTURE DIRECTIONS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A49": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_710_09\" id=\"tag_17_710_09\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
